{{Quote|We've never been to Raxus before.''"<br />"''The coordinates from Cid have us landing outside the capital city of Raxulon, the home of their Senate.|"[[Wrecker]]" and "[[Tech]]"|<ref name="Common Ground" />}}
'''Raxulon''' was the [[capital]] [[city]] of [[Raxus Secundus]],<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> an [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]]<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> that served as the capital of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. The [[Separatist Senate Building]] was located in Raxulon. As the [[Galactic Senate]] discussed the [[Republic military enhancement bill]], [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] visited Raxulon to discuss peace talks with Amidala's friend and [[Separatist Senate|Separatist Senator]] [[Mina Bonteri]].<ref name="Heroes" /> During the war, the city was thriving and had [[B1-series battle droid]]s guarding the landing platforms.<ref name="PoP">{{StoryCite|story=Pursuit of Peace (short story)|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Raxulon first appeared in "[[Heroes on Both Sides]]," the tenth episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]], which aired on [[November 19]], [[2010]].<ref name="Heroes Old EG">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode310.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Heroes on Both Sides}}</ref> It was not identified until the [[2015]] novel ''[[Dark Disciple]]'', written by [[Christie Golden]] and adapted from an unfinished eight-episode story arc for ''The Clone Wars'', written by [[Katie Lucas]], [[Matt Michnovetz]], and [[Dave Filoni]].<ref name="Dark Disciple" />

